] [17592186423586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423586 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423586 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423586 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186423566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423586 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f00c50c9-3345-5470-8ccb-bce50ca0fdd4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423587 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423583 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423587 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139967" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423587 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423587 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ \\sqrt{74}\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖2v‖.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423587 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "107fc4e1-2e72-5e57-99ba-69f5d3ed0685" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423587 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kv‖=|k|\\cdot ‖v‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2v‖ & =|2|\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(\\sqrt{74})^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{9+25+36+74} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{144} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423588 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423588 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74112" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423588 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423588 #edb/ref 1071 "Given $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖a‖.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423588 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "203f62af-5fb6-55c0-adc4-39591e34a84e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423588 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖a‖ & =\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423589 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423589 #edb/ref 1069 "q-39763" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423589 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423589 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the distance between the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423589 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3e3e1b93-57b0-53a0-86f4-45d076c9cfad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423589 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,0) & =‖x-0‖ \\\\  & =‖x‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-18)^{2}+(-12)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+324+144+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{529} \\\\  & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423590 #edb/ref 1069 "q-39217" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423590 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423590 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2k\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ k \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find $k$, if the distance between the vectors is $\\text{d}(x,y)=\\sqrt{83}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423590 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "48de0343-fd7b-5b5e-947b-c8f60a378766" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423590 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we calculate the distance between $x$ and $y$ in terms of $k:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{y}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(k-0)^{2}+(0-k)^{2}+((-1)-(-2))^{2}+(-2k-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{k}^{2}+{k}^{2}+{1}^{2}+4{k}^{2}+8k+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}+8k+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $\\text{d}(x,y)=\\sqrt{83},$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}+8k+5} & =\\sqrt{83} \\\\ {(\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}+8k+5})}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{83})}^{2} \\\\ 6{k}^{2}+8k+5 & =83 \\\\ 6{k}^{2}+8k-78 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the quadratic formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{{8}^{2}-4(6)(-78)}}{2(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{1\\,936}}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm 44}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\pm 11}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives $k=3$ and $k=-\\frac{13}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423591 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423591 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74146" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423591 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423591 #edb/ref 1071 "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423591 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6fe81e21-b32f-5653-9746-86ee81aa65aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423591 #edb/ref 1074 "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{-1}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423592 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423592 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74130" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423592 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423592 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖4v‖.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423592 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8cc596a5-8803-52b2-93a7-a243d5af26bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423592 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kv‖=|k|\\cdot ‖v‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖4v‖ & =|4|\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{1+9+1+9} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423593 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423593 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74149" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423593 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423593 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $k$, if $u=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{k}{4}\\end{aligned}]$ is a unit vector." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423593 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c46599f-15c6-531f-94db-06b03ec04f84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423593 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we calculate the norm of the vector $u$ in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{u}_{1}^{2}+{u}_{2}^{2}+{u}_{3}^{2}+{u}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}+{(\\frac{k}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{16}+\\frac{9}{16}+\\frac{{k}^{2}}{16}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14+{k}^{2}}{16}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $‖u‖=1,$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{14+{k}^{2}}{16}} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{14+{k}^{2}} & =4 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{14+{k}^{2}})}^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ 14+{k}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =2 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423594 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423594 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74118" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423594 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423594 #edb/ref 1071 "Given $w=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖w‖.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423594 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a076c01e-29ae-51f5-9ba7-a79f626ba8b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423594 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖w‖ & =\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}+{w}_{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{9}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(\\sqrt{10})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1+81+4+10} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423595 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423595 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74119" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423595 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423595 #edb/ref 1071 "Given $x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖x‖.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423595 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a59db3f3-f5cf-55e8-a066-a483320cdf58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423595 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}+{x}_{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9+64+9+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]