& =\\sqrt{39}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423600 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423600 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74132" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423600 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423600 #edb/ref 1071 "If $‖-2x‖=3$, find $‖6x‖.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423600 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eca368ca-a4ba-5312-b178-c63c0431130b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423600 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kx‖=|k|\\cdot ‖x‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-2x‖ & =3 \\\\ |-2|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =3 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $‖6x‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖6x‖ & =6\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
